# Conformance probe pack for rulings 16, 19 and 22 of spec 0.8, most
# significant bit first. Public. No kinds.
#
#   byte 0      n
#   byte 1      presence p.1 to p.3, then 5 unused bits
#   byte 2      w, and on the same bits val through the table `t`, and qty
#   1 bit       whether x follows; x in 8 bits
#   8 bits      y
#   p.1         z in 8 bits unless p.2 is 1, then the constant 170
#   p.2         c1 in 8 bits
#   p.3         a length in bytes, then: the constant 1 in 7 bits, an
#               extension bit, one bit that says whether c2 follows, c2 in 7 bits
#
# val and qty have a default and w has none: when the entity holds none of
# the three, the byte is the default of val (ruling 16). The default of y is
# written inside the `opt` block and is the message's (ruling 19).
format     conformance-seq-rulings-b
version    0.8.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.n  8  uint
presence p 3
pad 5
field   probe.w  8  uint
also    probe.val  via t
also    probe.qty
default probe.val  200
default probe.qty  9
opt
  field  probe.x  8  uint
  default probe.y  5
end
field   probe.y  8  uint
if p.1
  if !p.2
    field  probe.z  8  uint
  end
  const 8 170
end
if p.2
  field  probe.c1  8  uint
end
if p.3
  length 8
    chain
      const 7 1
      fx
      opt
        field  probe.c2  7  uint
      end
    end
  end
end
map     t  1  100
map     t  2  200
